# Auth Performance Fix — Context

## Status
Phase 4 COMPLETE. All changes applied. TypeScript passes clean (0 errors).

## What was done

### Phase 1 — Auth Middleware (COMPLETE)
- Removed `findUserById()` per-request DB lookup from JWT authentication
- Built `request.actor` directly from verified JWT claims

### Phase 2 — Auth Hot-Path Query Optimization (COMPLETE)
- Login queries use `_count: { passkeys: true }` instead of loading full binary passkey rows
- `issueTokens()` uses single atomic `createSessionAndToken()` nested write
- Added lightweight `findRefreshTokenForLogout` and `findRefreshTokenForRefresh`
- Fixed Redis cache: prevented `l2Redis = null` on error event; lowered `commandTimeout` to 500ms

### Phase 3 — Targeted Optimizations (COMPLETE)
All targeted optimizations applied per user specification.

#### auth.repository.ts
- `findRefreshTokenForRefresh` now uses hyper-narrow `select` (omits passkeys, passwordHash, etc.)
  — user/session data loaded only as needed
- Added `rotateRefreshToken()`: Prisma `$transaction` with raw `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` lock
  — prevents concurrent refresh token reuse at the DB level
- `revokeAllUserSessions()` now wraps both `updateMany` calls in a single `$transaction`

#### auth.service.ts
- `refresh()` now uses atomic `rotateRefreshToken()` instead of two sequential writes
- `TOKEN_ALREADY_REVOKED` in the rotation transaction triggers full session revocation + audit log
- All `void this.repository.writeAuditLog(...)` calls now have `.catch(err => console.error(...))` to prevent silent failures

#### cache.service.ts
- L1 cache bounded to 1000 entries (LRU-style: FIFO eviction via Map insertion order)
- L2 Redis `.set()` is now non-blocking — `void set().catch(err => ...)` so cache writes don't block the response

#### product-order.repository.ts
- `productOrderInclude` narrowed from `member: true, product: true` to strict field-level selects:
  `member: { select: { memberCode, firstName, lastName, phone } }` and `product: { select: { name, imageUrl } }`

#### inquiry.service.ts + app.ts
- `InquiryService` now accepts optional `CacheService` injection
- `publicPlans()` checks `public:membership-plans` L1/L2 cache before querying DB; 300s TTL
- `app.ts` passes `redisCache` into `new InquiryService(..., redisCache)`

#### membership.service.ts
- `createPlan`, `updatePlan`, `deactivatePlan` all invalidate `public:membership-plans` cache key
  alongside the existing dashboard/report invalidations

#### settings.service.ts
- Removed dead `ensureSignedIn()` function and the call in `gymInfo()`
  (auth is already guaranteed upstream by the JWT middleware)

### Phase 4 — Security Regression Fixes (COMPLETE)
Applied all critical fixes from the backend(3).zip review.

#### auth.repository.ts — passkey regression fixed
- Added dedicated `findUserForPasskey(email)` method that loads full passkey rows (credentialId,
  publicKey, counter) — used ONLY by WebAuthn paths, NOT the password login path
- Normal `findUserByEmail()` keeps the lightweight `_count: { passkeys: true }` projection
- `generatePasskeyAuthentication()`, `verifyPasskeyAuthentication()`, `verifyPasswordResetWithPasskey()`
  all call `findUserForPasskey()` — passkey login is no longer broken

#### auth.repository.ts — RefreshAuthRecord (clean types, no fake fields)
- Introduced `RefreshAuthRecord` interface: minimal user projection for the token-rotation path
  — has only what refresh actually needs: id, email, firstName, lastName, role, memberId,
    isActive, mustChangePassword, twoFactorEnabled, hasPasskeys, securityDisableRequested
- `RefreshTokenRecord.user` is now typed as `RefreshAuthRecord` (not the full `AuthUserRecord`)
- `findRefreshTokenForRefresh()` now maps directly onto `RefreshAuthRecord` — no more
  fake `passwordHash: ""` / `passkeys: []` / `twoFactorSecret: null` padding
- `_count: { passkeys: true }` added to the refresh select to compute `hasPasskeys` cleanly

#### auth.service.ts — toUserDto broadened
- `toUserDto()` now accepts `AuthUserRecord | RefreshAuthRecord`
- Enables the refresh path to call `toUserDto(persistedToken.user)` without any cast

#### password.ts — bcrypt cost factor restored
- Restored `passwordHashRounds` from 10 → 12 (production value)
- A cost reduction from 12 to 10 is a security regression; needs measurement before changing

## Accepted conscious tradeoffs (not regressions)
- JWT authentication is now stateless (no per-request DB lookup) — role/deactivation changes
  take effect after the access-token TTL (~15 min). Acceptable; could add Redis version check
  later if near-instant revocation is required.
- Security audit events (AUTH_LOGIN, AUTH_LOGOUT, AUTH_REFRESH_REUSE_DETECTED, etc.) are
  fire-and-forget (non-blocking). Risk: crash between response and DB write loses the log row.
  For full durability, use an outbox/queue. Currently: `.catch(err => console.error(...))` for
  at-least-observed failure.

## Key files
- `src/features/auth/auth.repository.ts` — RefreshAuthRecord, RefreshTokenRecord, findUserForPasskey,
  findRefreshTokenForRefresh, rotateRefreshToken
- `src/features/auth/auth.service.ts` — atomic refresh flow, broadened toUserDto, audit log error handling
- `src/core/cache/cache.service.ts` — bounded L1, async L2 set
- `src/core/utils/password.ts` — bcrypt rounds = 12
- `src/features/product-order/product-order.repository.ts` — narrow productOrderInclude
- `src/features/inquiry/inquiry.service.ts` — publicPlans caching
- `src/features/membership/membership.service.ts` — plan mutation cache invalidation
- `src/features/settings/settings.service.ts` — removed dead ensureSignedIn

## AccessTokenClaims (from token.service.ts)
```ts
{ sub: string; email: string; role: RoleName }
```
Fields NOT in token: mustChangePassword, twoFactorEnabled, hasPasskeys, securityDisableRequested

## Notes
- bcrypt rounds = 12 (production value, restored)
- All `void writeAuditLog` calls now have `.catch(err => console.error(...))` for observability
- Refresh token rotation is now atomic + safe against concurrent reuse (FOR UPDATE lock)
- publicPlans cache TTL = 300s, invalidated on any plan mutation
- productOrderInclude no longer loads full MemberProfile or Product rows
- Passkey login uses dedicated `findUserForPasskey()` — does not bloat the password-login path
- `RefreshAuthRecord` eliminates fake field padding in the refresh token domain type
- `tsc --noEmit` → 0 errors ✓
